  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Two unlicensed treasure hunters dug up a Bronze Age sky map. A bronze plate thirty centimetres wide, studded with gold stars.",
        "visual_query": "german hilltop forest excavation site",
        "visual_fallback": "forested hilltop"
      },
      {
        "narration": "They had no permit, so they sold it the next day for thirty-one thousand marks. It disappeared into the black market and kept changing hands.",
        "visual_query": "bronze age gold artifact closeup",
        "visual_fallback": "gold artifact"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Think about what was being passed around. Something made thirty-six hundred years ago, traded by dealers who could not read a mark on it.",
        "visual_query": "saxony anhalt countryside rolling hills",
        "visual_fallback": "german countryside"
      },
      {
        "narration": "In 2002 a state archaeologist posed as a buyer in a Basel hotel. Police took the disc back. The sellers had wanted seven hundred thousand marks for it.",
        "visual_query": "basel switzerland old city street",
        "visual_fallback": "swiss city"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Then the scientists read it. Seven dots are the Pleiades, and the gold arcs on the rim mark exactly where the sun sets at the solstices.",
        "visual_query": "night sky pleiades star cluster",
        "visual_fallback": "starry night"
      }
    ],
